speechtext:
The word ' limes ' is eliminated from this item. That is the reason the item is inserted here.
101a. Limes:	British preferential, free;
intermediate, 10 per cent; general, ten per cent.

The new rates are three-quarters of a cent less on the British preferential tariff, and the same on the general tariff.
111. Cocoannts. when imported from the place of growth, by ship, direct to a Canadian port, per one hundred:	British preference, free;
intermediate, 50 cents; general, 50 cents.

How much do you import from Germany and how much from Great Britain?
Mr-. WHITE: Raw sugar, 1912, imported under the.general tariff, 204,000,000 pounds;
under the preferential tariff, 358,000,000 pounds.
